abstract: >-
  Python implementation of Modular Time Field Theory (MTFT), deriving
  fundamental constants (alpha, alpha_s, sin^2 theta_W) from the
  arithmetic weights w_n = sum_{d|n} (log d)/d and the modular curve
  X_0(143). Ships a falsifiability engine with 23 zero-parameter,
  pre-registered predictions (run mtft.falsify.honest_report() for the
  live scorecard), a lattice gauge sector, and the three-ensemble
  Riemann toolkit: Laplace stiffness with the exact filtered moment
  identity, the Dirichlet ensemble Z_D(beta) = -zeta(beta) zeta'(beta+1)
  with its Speiser-Hadamard lab, and the critical ensemble computing
  Li coefficients by three cross-certified methods.
